	<key>readme</key>
	<string># English Sentence Mining

## First-time setup

1. Install OpenAI Codex CLI if it is not installed.
2. Run `ewsetup` in Alfred.
3. A Terminal window opens the Codex ChatGPT login flow.
4. Run `ewsetup` again. Success looks like: `Codex 已登录：/Users/you/.codex-ew`.

The workflow uses an isolated Codex home by default:

`~/.codex-ew`

This keeps the `ew` login/cache separate from your main Codex setup. To reuse your normal Codex login, change `codex_home` to:

`~/.codex`

## Default Codex lookup

- Model: `gpt-5.3-codex-spark`
- Service tier: default
- Reasoning effort: `low`

These values are editable in this Configure Workflow panel. For `gpt-5.5`, you may set Service Tier to `fast` and Reasoning Effort to `none`.

## Daily use

Select an English sentence, run Universal Actions, choose `ew`, then pick the unknown word or phrase. Manual fallback: type `ew &lt;sentence&gt;`.

`ew` shows sentence translation at the top of Alfred results. Exact word queries and `/phrase` queries warm target meaning previews in the background.

## Sharing safety

Do not export or publish `~/.codex/auth.json`, `~/.codex-ew/auth.json`, `config.json` with API keys, or any exported credential variables. Other users should run `ewsetup` and sign in with their own ChatGPT account.</string>
